<title>JAPAN: Japan May pork imports plunge 63.5 pct yr/yr--MOF.</title>
<headline>Japan May pork imports plunge 63.5 pct yr/yr--MOF.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's pork imports in May totalled 34,285 tonnes, down by 63.5 percent from a year earlier, Finance Ministry data released on Friday showed. </p>
<p>The details were as follows (in tonnes):</p>
<p>		     May 97	Apr 97	 May 96</p>
<p> Total	     34,285	41,975	 94,022</p>
<p> Refrigerated    13,484	10,813	 19,269</p>
<p> Frozen	    20,801	31,162	 74,753</p>
<p>Major suppliers of refrigerated pork (in tonnes):</p>
<p> Taiwan		 nil	   nil	   8,445</p>
<p> U.S.		10,327	 8,564	   9,405</p>
<p> Canada	     2,073	 1,222	     913</p>
<p>Major suppliers of frozen pork (in tonnes):</p>
<p>		     May 97	Apr 97	  May 96</p>
<p> Taiwan		  31	 5,635	  14,409</p>
<p> U.S.		 3,850	 3,476	  12,718</p>
<p> Denmark	    7,729	12,188	  31,104</p>
<p> Canada	     3,394	 3,474	   5,312</p>
<p> U.K.		   796	 1,371	   1,633</p>
<p> South Korea	1,832	 1,903	   3,348</p>
<p>Total imports of refrigerated pork in the first five months of calendar 1997 totalled 53,930 tonnes, against 68,764 tonnes in the same period a year earlier.</p>
<p>Total imports of frozen pork in the January-May period of this year totalled 99,390 tonnes, against 224,680 tonnes a year earlier, ministry data showed.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Commodities Desk +81-3-3432-7391</p>
</text>
